UNCalendarNotificationTrigger hands its DateComponents to SkipUI as `Any`, which the bridge cannot carry to Kotlin, so scheduling one is a fatal error; pending requests come back with a push trigger instead of their own; and the interruption level is missing. The components now cross as named Int values with their time zone (`dateComponents` is typed, as on iOS), pending requests carry their time-interval or calendar trigger with the date it fires, and the interruption level reaches SkipUI. Needs skip-ui 0017. Proposed upstream.

